{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552155-what-made-you-like-particular-clan-over-the-rest","id":1552155,"title":"What made you like particular clan over the rest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-07T11:46:50-07:00","id":1552155,"title":"What made you like particular clan over the rest?","content":"I'm curious what made you like a specific clan or bloodline over the others?<br /> <br /> As you know I'm a fan of the Malkavians as I like seers and prophets who can use the truth as a weapon and their Disciplines make them excellent intelligence gathers.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set/Ministry I like because of them being wildcards in any game and you never really know what kind of advantage they are truly getting. Also the Egyptian themes and disciplines that enable them to make friends is quite useful.<br /> <br /> So what drew you to your particular clans and why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T13:50:33-07:00","id":1552164,"title":"","content":"My first game was dark ages and I really vibbed the morbis but spiritual gothic vibe of clan cappadocian. I also had a massive crush on Serena from reception.<br /> <br /> You can imagine my annoyance when someone ran modern nights for me and I found out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T16:52:22-07:00","id":1552171,"title":"","content":"Haven't you already made two other threads with variations of this same question, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a>? I'm almost sure this isn't the first time, and that at least once it was you.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I like most clans for several reasons, so my list varies with my mood, but the Malkavians are usually on the top, or at least top 3, together with the Salubri.<br /> <br /> Some clans had several changes through time, so I like some versions (usually <i>Revised</i>) and not others. Followers of Set, Tzimisce and Banu Haqim are very strong in this regard. I don't know enough of the Ministry to say if it was a good idea or not, but overall I like the more nuanced versions of the Setites, particularly their less crazy DA versions. I don't have anything against Vicissitude as a Discipline, but overall I like the Old Clan take on the Tzimisce. I'm not a fan of <i>Necroscope</i>. And the Banu Haqim got a lot better with the passing of the years, and I like their Camarilla version from <i>Revised</i>, even if not so much Ur-Shulgi and his lackeys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T18:04:05-07:00","id":1552179,"title":"","content":"I might've.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T03:01:12-07:00","id":1552193,"title":"","content":"In a word? SNOBBERY.<br /> <br /> Whilst other Clans have their features of interest, Clan Ventrue has always had IMMENSE Christopher Lee energy* and I like to see that in a vampire.<br /> <br /> Also, y\u2019know, money, organisation <i>and</i> power.<br /> <br /> (It didn\u2019t hurt that the Clan of Kings traditionally has a deeply pragmatic approach to organising their immediate vicinity which I do appreciate).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>As opposed to Big Dracula Energy, which the Tzimisce have in spades: unfortunately the Body Horror thing isn\u2019t my cup of tea and their Clan Name just doesn\u2019t strike me as euphonious.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T07:29:56-07:00","id":1552281,"title":"","content":"I like all the Clans so its usually what I feel like at the moment when the question is posed. Right now I like Brujah and Toreador for their connection to ancient Greece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T11:08:22-07:00","id":1552290,"title":"","content":"I like Setites for the religious mysticism and the snake themes - not particularly the corruption and temptation, except when explained philosophically. My favourite iteration is by far VDA20, with the Warriors of Glycon and Witches of Echidna thrown in. I like elements from Revised, V20 and Dark Ages: Vampire as well. VDA20 Serpentis is so good for me that I actually get sad and disappointed when I think of playing them in V20.<br /> <br /> I like Banu Haqim because they're more elegant, pragmatic, honest and balanced than the rest of the clans. Their policing vampires, in as far as it is based on protecting the kine, is totally justified in my view - although the specifics depend on the edition. Their division in three functional - albeit competing - castes is also a hallmark of organisation and versatility most other clans lack. My favourite iteration is V20, especially how Quietus changes by caste (I'm in awe of how they managed to adapt the powers to the spirit of each caste while keeping all three with the same Discipline). I don't particularly like the VDA20 Viziers' branch of Quietus (the idea is fine, but the powers don't excite me), but I love that the Warriors' Quietus Cruscitus is Willpower based and that the Road of the Blood grants Aura bonuses to Willpower rolls, because it sinergises with both Warriors (Quietus Cruscitus) and Sorcerers (Thaumaturgy non-ritual rolls), and I'd have encouraged doing a sinergy with the Viziers' Quietus as well.<br /> <br /> I like Giovanni because they're hyper efficient, using mortals, their resources and influences, their corpses, their ghosts... everything. I once made a character in V20 with merits from the Nagaraja spread who would consume a victim's blood, flesh and bones, and I obviously hope he would learn the Viscuous Path in due time to consume even the hectoplasm of ghosts. Or maybe Im getting confused and he was a Nagaraja. Sorry, can't remember. I did make a few cannibalistic Giovanni, so it's hard to keep track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T00:22:51-07:00","id":1552323,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce Clan ended up becoming my favourite due to their emphasis on change and evolution. More than any other Clan, they defy the idea of vampires as unchanging beings, making an effort to become more than what they were at the time of their Embrace, or shifting the culture of their Clan as a whole in response to their circumstances, an idea reflected by the more mystical and isolated Methuselahs of their line choosing to Embrace medieval warlords in order to address the weaknesses of their existing culture. The Dracon may be my favourite Methesulah for the way that it's depicted as extending the concept of Metamorphosis to the wider world, beyond the existence of individual vampires. Even if you reject some of the more self-centred aspects of the Path, the way that the Path/Road of Metamorphosis focuses on an individualistic approach to the pursuit of personal perfection makes it interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T16:31:58-07:00","id":1552430,"title":"","content":"Love the Ventrue, Lasombra, Tzimisce and Giovonni. The history of them all, the clan disciplines and overall feel on how they control the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T08:38:19-07:00","id":1552559,"title":"","content":"The darkness itself of the Lasombra, that's it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}